{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall count them.</b> He returned to say so and was not satisfied with what He had said earlier, <b>Lift up the head</b> etc., in order to alert you to the intent of His saying <b>se'u</b>, in accordance with the words of the Sages of blessed memory (Yalkut Shimoni, Numbers 1) who said that the nations of the world grew jealous of Israel — what did they see to merit drawing near etc. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to them: Bring Me your books of genealogy (sefarim ikonin), and it turned out that none of them knew from which family he was — end quote. We see that HaShem insists on lineage, and anyone lacking a book of genealogy is debased. Therefore, when HaShem came to command the counting of Israel, He prefaced by saying <b>se'u</b> — a term of chieftaincy and exaltation — to find for each person a book of genealogy, which is not so among the nations of the world. And afterward He explained what the distinction is: <b>from twenty years old</b> etc., <b>you shall count them</b> — and from this point on, the expression is needed for its own sake."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:52.230278706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}